  "final_message": "I can't remove `channel` from the `OrderPlaced` event as asked, so I haven't changed anything.\n\nARCH-4 says `OrderPlaced` is consumed by billing-service and analytics-ingest, which live in other repositories. Changes to it must be additive, and removals have to go through deprecation. Dropping `channel` from the event could break a deployed consumer. I can't see those repos, so I can't check whether either one reads the field. Your note that `channel` is \"no longer read\" may only hold for this service.\n\nHere are some ways to proceed:\n\n1. **Deprecate first (my suggestion).** Keep `channel` on the event and mark it `@deprecated` in `src/core/events.ts`. Confirm with the billing-service and analytics-ingest owners that neither reads it, then remove it in a later change. In the meantime I can stop requiring `channel` on input and remove it from the internal order model. To keep the event field populated, I'd give it a fixed placeholder value or make it optional.\n2. **Remove it everywhere now.** If you've already confirmed with both consumer teams that nothing depends on it, tell me and I'll remove it from the event, the order model, request parsing, validation, the tests and the docs.\n3. **Remove it from the order model only.** The event would still carry `channel`, but there'd be no source for the value. It would have to be a placeholder, which is the same as option 1.\n\nWhich would you like?",
